  "paraphrase": "She is the clairvoyant daughter of one of Europe’s longest-reigning monarchs, while he is a self-described sixth-generation shaman from California. Their wedding on Saturday afternoon in Geiranger was far from a typical royal ceremony, yet crowds still gathered along the cloudy streets in hopes of seeing the bride. Märtha Louise, the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, is 52 and sits fourth in line to the Norwegian throne. She wed Verrett, 49, in a traditional church service at the four-star Hotel Union in a small village below the Geiranger fjord, with royals and celebrities among the guests. The princess was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her first marriage to the late Norwegian writer Ari Behn, whom she divorced in 2017. The 350 guests also included her brother, Crown Prince Haakon, and his wife, Crown Princess Mette-Marit; Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel; and the Netherlands’ Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien. Märtha Louise has long lived outside the bounds of conventional royalty, having previously said she was clairvoyant and spent 10 years running a healing school that taught people how to communicate with angels. In 2022, she said she would give up official royal duties in order to concentrate on her and Verrett’s business and to make the distinction between their work and the Norwegian royal family clearer. Verrett, meanwhile, describes himself on Instagram as a “servant of God” and an “energy activator,” and among his best-known clients is Goop founder Gwyneth Paltrow, whom he has referred to as a “soul sister.”"
}

